---

<div class="pl-pig not-content">
  <!-- Walkthrough: session evidence → finding → proposed fix → reviewed release.
       Without JavaScript every step and panel renders stacked, in order. The
       script below upgrades the list into an ARIA tablist with roving tabindex. -->
  <section
    id="pig-walkthrough"
    class="pl-pig-section"
    aria-labelledby="pig-walkthrough-title"
    data-section-tracked="agent-learning-loop"
  >
    <header class="pl-pig-heading">
      <h2 id="pig-walkthrough-title">One repeated correction becomes a reviewed fix.</h2>
      <p>
        Follow a single example: Acme’s <code>review-docs</code> skill tells agents to verify every code example, but never says which product version to verify against.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="pl-pig-walkthrough" data-pig-walkthrough>
      <ol class="pl-pig-steps" data-pig-steps aria-label="Walkthrough steps">
        {steps.map((step, index) => (
          <li>
            <button
              type="button"
              class:list={['pl-pig-step', { 'is-active': index === 0 }]}
              id={`pig-step-tab-${step.id}`}
              data-pig-step={step.id}
              aria-controls={`pig-step-panel-${step.id}`}
            >
              <span class="pl-pig-step-num">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
              <span class="pl-pig-step-text">
                <span class="pl-pig-step-label">{step.label}</span>
                <span class="pl-pig-step-summary">{step.summary}</span>
              </span>
            </button>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>

      <div class="pl-pig-panels">
        <div class="pl-pig-panel" id="pig-step-panel-evidence" data-pig-panel="evidence" aria-labelledby="pig-step-tab-evidence">
          <div class="pl-pig-ui">
            <div class="pl-pig-ui-bar">
              <span class="pl-pig-ui-title">Session · Claude Code · docs team</span>
              <span class="pl-pig-example-tag">Example</span>
            </div>
            <div class="pl-pig-ui-body">
              <ol class="pl-pig-transcript">
                <li><span class="pl-pig-role">user</span><p>Update the SDK quickstart for the v3 release.</p></li>
                <li><span class="pl-pig-role pl-pig-role-agent">agent</span><p>Checked every example against <code>acme-sdk 2.9</code>. All examples pass.</p></li>
                <li class="pl-pig-transcript-flag"><span class="pl-pig-role">user</span><p>Those are v2 calls. This page documents v3.</p></li>
                <li><span class="pl-pig-role pl-pig-role-agent">agent</span><p>Sorry, re-checking against <code>acme-sdk 3.0</code>…</p></li>
              </ol>
